  +#207#142#206#189';"'#10#10'#: formconfig.rresponsehint'#10'msgid ""'#10'"Jso'
  +'n Pointer: Use / for levels, keys for objects, and numbers for indexes.\n"'
  +#10'"Use * for all items, *#10 to join items by newline. Use ~ at the end of'
  +' the path to return the raw JSON branch.\n"'#10'"Separate multiple segments'
  +' with semicolon ;.\n"'#10'"Literal: Text block in {'#226#128#166'}. Special'
  +' tag #10 for newlines. Use {{regex}} inside to extract data directly into t'
  +'he text.\n"'#10'"Logic: If a Pointer in a segment is empty, the whole segme'
  +'nt is skipped. If a segment has no Pointer, only literal text blocks with e'
  +'mbedded regular expressions are processed.\n"'#10'"Regex: {prefix {regex[in'
  +'dex]} suffix} inside a text block. If no [index] is specified, the first ma'
  +'tch is used.\n"'#10'"Index can be a number, [*] (join by space), or [*#10] '
  +'(join by newline). If the regex finds no match, the entire {'#226#128#166'}'
  +' block is removed.\n"'#10'"Using ~ inside a regex returns the entire text.\'
  +'n"'#10'"Inversion: Start a segment with ! (e.g. !/path{Error}) to show its '
  +'text only if the Pointer data is missing or the JSON is invalid.\n"'#10'"Co'
