  +#176#224#165#141#224#164#164#224#164#168' '#224#164#184#224#164#185#224#165
  +#135#224#164#156#224#165#135#224#164#130'?"'#10#10'#: formconfig.rresponsehi'
  +'nt'#10'msgid ""'#10'"Json Pointer: Use / for levels, keys for objects, and '
  +'numbers for indexes.\n"'#10'"Use * for all items, *#10 to join items by new'
  +'line. Use ~ at the end of the path to return the raw JSON branch.\n"'#10'"S'
  +'eparate multiple segments with semicolon ;.\n"'#10'"Literal: Text block in '
  +'{'#226#128#166'}. Special tag #10 for newlines. Use {{regex}} inside to ext'
  +'ract data directly into the text.\n"'#10'"Logic: If a Pointer in a segment '
  +'is empty, the whole segment is skipped. If a segment has no Pointer, only l'
  +'iteral text blocks with embedded regular expressions are processed.\n"'#10
  +'"Regex: {prefix {regex[index]} suffix} inside a text block. If no [index] i'
  +'s specified, the first match is used.\n"'#10'"Index can be a number, [*] (j'
  +'oin by space), or [*#10] (join by newline). If the regex finds no match, th'
  +'e entire {'#226#128#166'} block is removed.\n"'#10'"Using ~ inside a regex '
  +'returns the entire text.\n"'#10'"Inversion: Start a segment with ! (e.g. !/'
  +'path{Error}) to show its text only if the Pointer data is missing or the JS'
  +'ON is invalid.\n"'#10'"Commenting: /* text */ comments are stripped from th'
  +'e entire expression before any processing.\n"'#10'"Examples:\n"'#10'"respon'
  +'seData/translatedText; matches/*#10/translation; /texts/text; {literal text'
