  +#159'"'#10#10'#: formconfig.rresponsehint'#10'msgid ""'#10'"Json Pointer: Us'
  +'e / for levels, keys for objects, and numbers for indexes.\n"'#10'"Use * fo'
  +'r all items, *#10 to join items by newline. Use ~ at the end of the path to'
  +' return the raw JSON branch.\n"'#10'"Separate multiple segments with semico'
  +'lon ;.\n"'#10'"Literal: Text block in {'#226#128#166'}. Special tag #10 for'
  +' newlines. Use {{regex}} inside to extract data directly into the text.\n"'
  +#10'"Logic: If a Pointer in a segment is empty, the whole segment is skipped'
  +'. If a segment has no Pointer, only literal text blocks with embedded regul'
  +'ar expressions are processed.\n"'#10'"Regex: {prefix {regex[index]} suffix}'
  +' inside a text block. If no [index] is specified, the first match is used.\'
  +'n"'#10'"Index can be a number, [*] (join by space), or [*#10] (join by newl'
  +'ine). If the regex finds no match, the entire {'#226#128#166'} block is rem'
  +'oved.\n"'#10'"Using ~ inside a regex returns the entire text.\n"'#10'"Inver'
  +'sion: Start a segment with ! (e.g. !/path{Error}) to show its text only if '
  +'the Pointer data is missing or the JSON is invalid.\n"'#10'"Commenting: /* '
  +'text */ comments are stripped from the entire expression before any process'
  +'ing.\n"'#10'"Examples:\n"'#10'"responseData/translatedText; matches/*#10/tr'
  +'anslation; /texts/text; {literal text#10}; /result/text; /text{ ({(\\w+)})}'
  +'; !/translations{Error: No data!#10}; /translations/0/text"'#10'msgstr ""'
