  +#156#234#178#160#236#138#181#235#139#136#234#185#140'?"'#10#10'#: formconfig'
  +'.rresponsehint'#10'msgid ""'#10'"Json Pointer: Use / for levels, keys for o'
  +'bjects, and numbers for indexes.\n"'#10'"Use * for all items, *#10 to join '
  +'items by newline. Use ~ at the end of the path to return the raw JSON branc'
  +'h.\n"'#10'"Separate multiple segments with semicolon ;.\n"'#10'"Literal: Te'
  +'xt block in {'#226#128#166'}. Special tag #10 for newlines. Use {{regex}} i'
  +'nside to extract data directly into the text.\n"'#10'"Logic: If a Pointer i'
  +'n a segment is empty, the whole segment is skipped. If a segment has no Poi'
  +'nter, only literal text blocks with embedded regular expressions are proces'
  +'sed.\n"'#10'"Regex: {prefix {regex[index]} suffix} inside a text block. If '
  +'no [index] is specified, the first match is used.\n"'#10'"Index can be a nu'
  +'mber, [*] (join by space), or [*#10] (join by newline). If the regex finds '
  +'no match, the entire {'#226#128#166'} block is removed.\n"'#10'"Using ~ ins'
  +'ide a regex returns the entire text.\n"'#10'"Inversion: Start a segment wit'
  +'h ! (e.g. !/path{Error}) to show its text only if the Pointer data is missi'
  +'ng or the JSON is invalid.\n"'#10'"Commenting: /* text */ comments are stri'
  +'pped from the entire expression before any processing.\n"'#10'"Examples:\n"'
  +#10'"responseData/translatedText; matches/*#10/translation; /texts/text; {li'
  +'teral text#10}; /result/text; /text{ ({(\\w+)})}; !/translations{Error: No '
  +'data!#10}; /translations/0/text"'#10'msgstr ""'#10'"JSON Pointer: '#235#160
