  +'?"'#10#10'#: formconfig.rresponsehint'#10'msgid ""'#10'"Json Pointer: Use /'
  +' for levels, keys for objects, and numbers for indexes.\n"'#10'"Use * for a'
  +'ll items, *#10 to join items by newline. Use ~ at the end of the path to re'
  +'turn the raw JSON branch.\n"'#10'"Separate multiple segments with semicolon'
  +' ;.\n"'#10'"Literal: Text block in {'#226#128#166'}. Special tag #10 for ne'
  +'wlines. Use {{regex}} inside to extract data directly into the text.\n"'#10
  +'"Logic: If a Pointer in a segment is empty, the whole segment is skipped. I'
  +'f a segment has no Pointer, only literal text blocks with embedded regular '
  +'expressions are processed.\n"'#10'"Regex: {prefix {regex[index]} suffix} in'
  +'side a text block. If no [index] is specified, the first match is used.\n"'
  +#10'"Index can be a number, [*] (join by space), or [*#10] (join by newline)'
  +'. If the regex finds no match, the entire {'#226#128#166'} block is removed'
  +'.\n"'#10'"Using ~ inside a regex returns the entire text.\n"'#10'"Inversion'
  +': Start a segment with ! (e.g. !/path{Error}) to show its text only if the '
  +'Pointer data is missing or the JSON is invalid.\n"'#10'"Commenting: /* text'
  +' */ comments are stripped from the entire expression before any processing.'
